-- CK-04: the pending twin of the guard `tests/corpus/check/bad/TryDefaultCycle.beni`,
-- which `v2-expected.md` skips because its golden pins checker v1's place and
-- text (R5's structural review, S6): `y = x?` and then `y` and `x` in the
-- same position make `x`'s type contain itself, whichever shape `?` settles
-- on — ONE `infinite_type`, the `?` defaulted to `Result` and the cycle
-- reported, not silenced. Under checker v2 it is reported at the parameter
-- `x`, a binder (checker-v2.md §6.3, §8.2); checker v1 at 2bc9e22 reports it
-- at the body, so this is red on v1 and claimed under v2 until R11
-- re-blesses the guard.
f x =
    let
        y =
            x?
    in
    if True then
        y

    else
        x
